 {'GxVAEs': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method'], 'description': ['A novel deep generative model for de novo molecular generation, comprising two joint Variational Autoencoders (ProfileVAE and MolVAE), designed to generate hit-like molecules from gene expression profiles by incorporating disease-related cellular environments.', 'A novel deep generative model for de novo molecular generation, incorporating disease-related cellular environments (gene expression profiles) into the generation process.', 'A novel deep generative model for de novo molecular generation that incorporates disease-related cellular environments, specifically gene expression profiles, into the generation process. It comprises two joint Variational Autoencoders (VAEs): ProfileVAE and MolVAE.', 'A novel deep generative model for de novo molecular generation in computer-aided drug discovery, incorporating disease-related cellular environments (gene expression profiles) into the generation process.', 'A novel deep generative model for de novo molecular generation, comprising two joint Variational Autoencoders (ProfileVAE and MolVAE) that incorporate disease-related cellular environments (gene expression profiles) to generate biologically meaningful molecules.', 'A novel deep generative model for de novo molecular generation, incorporating disease-related cellular environments (gene expression profiles) into the generation process.', 'A novel deep generative model for de novo molecular generation, incorporating disease-related cellular environments (gene expression profiles) to generate biologically meaningful molecules. It comprises ProfileVAE and MolVAE.', 'A novel deep generative model for de novo molecular generation, comprising two joint Variational Autoencoders (ProfileVAE and MolVAE), designed to incorporate disease-related cellular environments (gene expression profiles) into the generation process to produce biologically meaningful molecules.', 'A novel deep generative model for de novo molecular generation, incorporating disease-related cellular environments (gene expression profiles) to produce biologically meaningful molecules with desired bioactivity and drug-likeness.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9]}, 'ProfileVAE': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method'], 'description': ['The first Variational Autoencoder (VAE) within GxVAEs, responsible for extracting latent features from gene expression profiles.', 'One of the two joint Variational Autoencoders (VAEs) in GxVAEs. It functions as a feature extractor, learning latent representations from gene expression profiles.', 'One of the two joint Variational Autoencoders (VAEs) in GxVAEs, acting as a feature extractor that learns latent representations from gene expression profiles.', 'One of the two joint Variational Autoencoders in GxVAEs, acting as a feature extractor to learn latent representations from gene expression profiles.', 'A component of GxVAEs that acts as a feature extractor, learning latent representations from gene expression profiles.', 'A component of GxVAEs that acts as a feature extractor, learning latent representations from gene expression profiles and proving the effectiveness of GxVAEs.', 'A component of GxVAEs that acts as a feature extractor, learning latent representations from gene expression profiles.', 'One of the two joint Variational Autoencoders in GxVAEs, responsible for acting as a feature extractor by learning latent representations from gene expression profiles.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]}, 'MolVAE': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method'], 'description': ['The second Variational Autoencoder (VAE) within GxVAEs, which is conditioned by features extracted from ProfileVAE to generate hit-like molecules.', 'One of the two joint Variational Autoencoders (VAEs) in GxVAEs. It generates hit-like molecules, conditioned by features extracted from gene expression profiles by ProfileVAE.', 'One of the two joint Variational Autoencoders (VAEs) in GxVAEs, which is conditioned by features extracted from gene expression profiles to generate hit-like molecules.', 'The second joint Variational Autoencoder in GxVAEs, conditioned on features extracted by ProfileVAE to generate hit-like molecules using non-canonical SMILES strings.', 'A component of GxVAEs that generates hit-like molecules, conditioned on features extracted by ProfileVAE.', 'A component of GxVAEs that generates hit-like molecules, conditioned by features extracted from gene expression profiles by ProfileVAE.', 'The second of the two joint Variational Autoencoders in GxVAEs, which takes features extracted by ProfileVAE as conditions to generate hit-like molecules.', 'One of the two joint Variational Autoencoders (VAEs) in GxVAEs, responsible for generating hit-like molecules, conditioned by features extracted from gene expression profiles.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9]}, 'Bioactivity': {'type': ['generic', 'generic'], 'description': ['The ability of a molecule to produce a biological effect, a desired property for molecules generated by GxVAEs.', 'A desired characteristic of molecules that deep generative models aim to achieve during the generation process.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1]}, 'Drug-Likeness': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['A set of desirable physicochemical properties that predict whether a compound will have good pharmacokinetic properties, a target characteristic for molecules generated by GxVAEs.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'Latent Features': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Abstract representations learned by ProfileVAE from gene expression profiles, used to guide the generation process in MolVAE.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'Omics-based approaches': {'type': ['METHOD'], 'description': ['Approaches to drug discovery that offer promising opportunities but require a deep understanding of underlying biological and disease mechanisms for interpretation.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Artificial intelligence (AI)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A field of computer science that enables the generation of new molecules with desired bioactivity for specific therapeutic targets through deep learning and computational chemistry.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Deep learning': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A subfield of machine learning that powers AI techniques for molecular generation, enabling the creation of new molecules with desired bioactivity.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Computational chemistry': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A scientific discipline that, combined with deep learning, enables AI techniques for molecular generation.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Generative adversarial networks (GANs)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A type of deep generative model used to accelerate the drug discovery process by employing computational models to generate molecules having a specific bioactivity.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Drug discovery': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The overall process of identifying and developing new medicines, which is being accelerated by AI techniques and deep generative models.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'TransVAE': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A deep generative model that produces molecules from SMILES strings using VAEs.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'GrammarVAE': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A deep generative model that produces molecules from SMILES strings using VAEs.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Biological System': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The broader context of biological systems whose cellular environment is considered by GxVAEs to make generated molecules more biologically meaningful.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'JTVAE': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A model that generates molecules from a molecular graph by first creating a tree-structured scaffold and then combining it into a molecule using a graphical message-passing network.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'MolGAN': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A discrete GAN that uses reinforcement learning to generate molecular graphs.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'TransORGAN': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A discrete GAN that uses reinforcement learning to generate SMILES strings.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'ExpressionGAN': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'method'], 'description': ['A GAN model that bridges systems biology and molecular design to produce molecules with a high probability of inducing desired transcriptome features automatically from gene expression profiles.', 'A baseline model for molecular generation that generates hit-like molecules with low validity and limited ability to reproduce known ligands, serving as a comparison point for GxVAEs.', 'A state-of-the-art baseline model for molecular generation, used for comparison with GxVAEs. It has limited ability to generate valid molecules.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 4, 7]}, 'TRIOMPHE': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'method'], 'description': ['A VAE-based model that first calculates the correlation of ligand-target interactions between chemically induced transcriptome profiles and gene perturbation transcriptome profiles, then uses a VAE to generate molecules with desired transcriptome profiles.', 'A baseline model for molecular generation that utilizes gene expression profiles only in correlation calculations, without its VAE being involved in molecular generation, serving as a comparison point for GxVAEs.', 'A state-of-the-art baseline model for molecular generation, used for comparison with GxVAEs. GxVAEs show higher validity and comparable novelty to TRIOMPHE.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 4, 7]}, 'Deep Generative Models': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A class of AI models used for de novo molecular generation, including GxVAEs, ExpressionGAN, and TRIOMPHE, which aim to produce biologically meaningful molecules.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'Transcriptome Profiles': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['Profiles reflecting cellular responses to molecular treatment or gene perturbations, used by models like TRIOMPHE to guide molecular generation.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'SMILES': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Simplified Molecular Input Line Entry System, a string notation for representing chemical structures. GxVAEs uses non-canonical SMILES, specifically variant SMILES, for molecular generation.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'Teacher Forcing': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A training technique used to stabilize the training and accelerate the convergence of the MolVAE component within GxVAEs during its training phase.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'AAAI-24': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The Thirty-Eighth AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, where the research on GxVAEs was presented.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'Validity': {'type': ['generic', 'task'], 'description': ['A metric used to evaluate the quality of generated molecules, referring to the proportion of chemically valid molecules produced. ExpressionGAN has low validity.', 'A metric used to evaluate the quality of generated molecules, indicating the proportion of chemically valid molecules. GxVAEs demonstrate significantly higher validity compared to TRIOMPHE.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 7]}, 'Uniqueness': {'type': ['generic', 'task'], 'description': ['A metric used to evaluate the diversity of generated molecules, referring to the proportion of distinct molecules produced.', 'A metric assessing the diversity of generated molecules, measuring the proportion of distinct molecules. GxVAEs generally exceed TRIOMPHE in uniqueness.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 7]}, 'Latent Variable': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ["An unobserved variable in the generative process of ProfileVAE, denoted by 'C', which captures essential features of the gene expression profiles."], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Likelihood Function': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['The probability of observing the gene expression profile given the latent variable, denoted as p_phi(X|C) for ProfileVAE.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Posterior Distribution': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['The probability distribution of the latent variable given the gene expression profile, denoted as q_theta(C|X) for ProfileVAE.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'LINCS L1000 Database': {'type': ['DATASET'], 'description': ['A database containing gene expression profiles from cellular experiments, used to collect chemically induced and target perturbation profiles.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'KL Divergence': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['A measure of how one probability distribution diverges from a second, expected probability distribution. Used in the loss function of ProfileVAE and MolVAE.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Chemically Induced Profiles': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['Gene expression profiles collected from experiments where cells are treated with various molecules, sourced from the LINCS L1000 database.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Target Perturbation Profiles': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['Gene expression profiles obtained by altering the activity of specific biological targets, sourced from the LINCS database.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'MCF7 Cell Line': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['A human breast cancer cell line used in experiments to generate chemically induced gene expression profiles.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'AKT1': {'type': ['generic', 'generic'], 'description': ['RAC-α serine/threonine-protein kinase, a therapeutic protein for cancers.', 'A specific target protein for which GxVAEs demonstrated significantly higher Tanimoto coefficients compared to baseline models.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6, 7]}, 'AKT2': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['RACβ serine/threonine-protein kinase, a therapeutic protein for cancers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'AURKB': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Aurora B kinase, a therapeutic protein for cancers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'CTSK': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Cysteine synthase A, a therapeutic protein for cancers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'EGFR': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Epidermal growth factor receptor, a therapeutic protein for cancers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'HDAC1': {'type': ['generic', 'generic'], 'description': ['Histone deacetylase 1, a therapeutic protein for cancers.', 'A target protein for which GxVAEs achieved a validity of at least 78.0% when generating ligand-like molecules.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6, 7]}, 'MTOR': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Mammalian target of rapamycin, a therapeutic protein for cancers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'PIK3CA': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase catalytic subunit, a therapeutic protein for cancers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'SMAD3': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Decapentaplegic homolog 3, a therapeutic protein for cancers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'TP53': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Tumor protein p53, a therapeutic protein for cancers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'CREEDS': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['Crowd extracted expression of differential signatures database, used for collecting disease-specific profiles.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'RDKit': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A cheminformatics toolkit used to verify the chemical validity of generated molecules.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'QED': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Quantitative estimate of drug-likeness, a metric that quantifies the likelihood that a molecule is a drug.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Novelty': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['A metric evaluating the originality of generated molecules, indicating how different they are from known molecules. GxVAEs show comparable novelty to TRIOMPHE.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'Target proteins': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Proteins for which GxVAEs generate candidate ligands. Gene expression profiles of ten target proteins were used in experiments.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'DRAGONET': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A baseline model used for comparison with GxVAEs, which also generates molecules from patient gene expression profiles and molecule chemical structures.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Atopic Dermatitis': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['A specific disease for which GxVAEs generated candidate therapeutic molecules, demonstrating a Tanimoto coefficient of 1.0 with hydrocortisone, indicating effective capture of structural features of approved drugs for this condition.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Gastric Cancer': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ["A disease for which GxVAEs generated molecules exhibiting structural similarities to known approved drugs, contributing to the model's demonstrated therapeutic potential."], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, "Alzheimer's Disease": {'type': ['task'], 'description': ["A disease for which GxVAEs generated molecules showing structural features similar to known approved drugs, highlighting the model's capability in generating therapeutically relevant compounds."], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Hydrocortisone': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['A known approved drug used as a reference point for evaluating the structural similarity of molecules generated by GxVAEs for atopic dermatitis.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Therapeutic Molecular Generation': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The overall process undertaken by GxVAEs to generate candidate therapeutic molecules by inputting disease reversal profiles into the model.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'latent space': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['The dimensionality of the representation learned by the VAEs, which can influence the diversity of generated molecules. A limitation of GxVAEs is that diversity may be influenced by its size.'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'latent vector': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['A fixed representation within the latent space that, if adopted by MolVAE, could potentially constrain the diversity of newly generated molecules.'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'molecular structures': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['The output of generative models like GxVAEs, representing potential drug candidates with therapeutic effects for various diseases.'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'disease profiles': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['Patient-specific data, including gene expression profiles, used to guide the generation of molecules with potential therapeutic effects for particular diseases.'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'De Novo Molecular Generation': {'description': ['The process of creating new molecules with desired chemical properties and biological activity, a key task in computer-aided drug discovery addressed by GxVAEs.', 'The process of producing new molecules with specific chemical properties, aiming to create biologically meaningful molecules that overcome limitations of traditional methods.', 'A promising approach in computer-aided drug discovery that uses artificial intelligence (AI) techniques to generate new molecules with desired bioactivity for specific therapeutic targets.'], 'type': ['METHOD', 'TASK'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2]}, 'High-Throughput Screening (HTS)': {'description': ['A traditional experimental approach used in drug discovery to identify hit molecules with desired bioactivity, contrasted with the AI-driven approach of GxVAEs.', 'A traditional experimental method in drug discovery that tends to have a relatively low hit rate and involves labor-intensive and time-consuming processes.'], 'type': ['METHOD'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1]}, 'Gene Expression Profiles': {'description': ['Biological data representing the activity of genes, used by GxVAEs to condition molecular generation and bridge the gap between molecular generation and cellular environments.', 'Biological data representing the activity of genes. GxVAEs uses these profiles, including chemically induced, target perturbation, and disease-specific profiles, to guide molecular generation.', 'Biological data representing the activity of genes, used to condition molecular generation in GxVAEs and guide the discovery of therapeutic molecules for specific diseases.'], 'type': ['dataset'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8]}, 'Computer-Aided Drug Discovery': {'description': ['A field that utilizes computational methods to aid in the discovery and design of new drugs, where GxVAEs is applied.', 'The field in which GxVAEs is introduced as a novel deep generative model for de novo molecular generation.', 'The field that utilizes computational methods, including deep generative models like GxVAEs, to accelerate the process of discovering new drugs.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2, 3]}, 'Hit Molecules': {'description': ['Molecules identified in drug discovery that exhibit desired bioactivity and therapeutic effects, which GxVAEs aims to generate.', 'Molecules generated by GxVAEs that are similar in structure to known ligands and possess desired bioactivity and drug-likeness.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 7]}, 'Cellular Environments': {'description': ['The surrounding conditions of cells, including gene expression profiles, which GxVAEs incorporates to generate biologically meaningful molecules.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 2]}, 'Variational autoencoders (VAEs)': {'description': ['A type of deep generative model used to accelerate the drug discovery process by employing computational models to generate molecules having a specific bioactivity.', 'A class of deep generative models that GxVAEs is based on, specifically utilizing two joint VAEs (ProfileVAE and MolVAE) for its functionality.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 2]}, 'Hit-like Molecules': {'description': ['Molecules that exhibit desired bioactivity and drug-likeness, which GxVAEs aims to generate.', 'Molecules generated by models like GxVAEs that exhibit desired bioactivity and drug-likeness, aiming to overcome the low hit rates of traditional experimental methods.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 4, 7, 8]}, 'SMILES Strings': {'description': ['Simplified Molecular Input Line Entry System strings, a data structure used for de novo molecular generation, which models like TransVAE and GrammarVAE utilize.', 'A string representation of molecular structures, used to evaluate the data distributions learned by GxVAEs. The generated SMILES strings were consistent with the original validation set.'], 'type': ['dataset'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 7]}, 'Tanimoto Coefficients': {'description': ['A similarity metric used to assess how structurally similar generated molecules are to known ligands, indicating relevance. GxVAEs show improved Tanimoto coefficients compared to baselines.', 'A measure used to quantify the structural similarity between generated molecules and known approved drugs, employed to evaluate the performance of GxVAEs and DRAGONET.', 'A measure of molecular similarity, used to compare the generated molecules with known ligands. GxVAEs achieve much higher Tanimoto coefficients than baseline models.'], 'type': ['task', 'generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [8, 4, 7]}}
