erforms current state-of-the-art baselines for computer-aided drug discovery objectives. ; GxVAEs outperforms current state-of-the-art baselines for computer-aided drug discovery objectives.', 'source_index': [0, 0, 0, 0], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'COMPUTER-AIDED DRUG DISCOVERY'}, {'weight': 8.857142857142858, 'description': "GxVAEs is designed to generate hit-like molecules from gene expression profiles. ; GxVAEs is designed to generate 'hit-like' molecules from gene expression profiles. ; GxVAEs generates hit-like molecules from gene expression profiles. ; GxVAEs generates hit-like molecules that show potential bioactivity and drug-likeness. ; GxVAEs are designed to generate 'hit-like' molecules. ; GxVAEs generates hit-like molecules. ; The chemical structures of the hit-like molecules generated by GxVAEs are all similar to the structures of the known ligands.", 'source_index': [0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 2, 2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'HIT-LIKE MOLECULES'}, {'weight': 9.0, 'description': "GxVAEs generates hit-like molecules from gene expression profiles. ; GxVAEs generates 'hit-like' molecules from gene expression profiles. ; GxVAEs generate molecules from gene expression profiles. ; GxVAEs generate molecules that are biologically meaningful in the context of specific diseases using gene expression profiles. ; GxVAEs generates hit-like molecules from gene expression profiles. ; GxVAEs generates molecules from Gene Expression Profiles.", 'source_index': [0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'GENE EXPRESSION PROFILES'}, {'weight': 9.5, 'description': 'GxVAEs leverages two joint variational autoencoders (VAEs). ; GxVAEs leverages two joint variational autoencoders (VAEs).', 'source_index': [0, 0], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'VARIATIONAL AUTOENCODERS (VAES)'}, {'weight': 8.0, 'description': 'GxVAEs bridges the gap between molecular generation and the cellular environment. ; GxVAEs bridges the gap between molecular generation and the cellular environment, making produced molecules biologically meaningful.', 'source_index': [0, 0], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'CELLULAR ENVIRONMENT'}, {'weight': 7.6, 'description': 'The text explicitly states that GxVAEs uses SMILES strings for de novo molecular generation. ; GxVAEs uses SMILES strings for de novo molecular generation. ; GxVAEs uses SMILES strings as a data structure for de novo molecular generation. ; GxVAEs uses SMILES strings for molecular representation. ; GxVAEs uses SMILES Strings as a representation method for molecular structures.', 'source_index': [0, 0, 0, 2, 2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'SMILES STRINGS'}, {'weight': 10.0, 'description': 'The text describes GxVAEs as a novel deep generative model. ; GxVAEs is described as a novel deep generative model.', 'source_index': [0, 0], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'DEEP GENERATIVE MODELS'}, {'weight': 8.5, 'description': 'GxVAEs generates hit-like molecules with potential bioactivity. ; GxVAEs generates hit-like molecules with potential bioactivity.', 'source_index': [0, 0], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'BIOACTIVITY'}, {'weight': 8.5, 'description': 'GxVAEs generates hit-like molecules with potential drug-like properties. ; GxVAEs generates hit-like molecules with potential drug-likeness.', 'source_index': [0, 0], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'DRUG-LIKENESS'}, {'weight': 8.5, 'description': 'GxVAEs consist of two joint VAEs, including ProfileVAE. ; GxVAEs leverages ProfileVAE.', 'source_index': [1, 2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'PROFILEVAE'}, {'weight': 8.5, 'description': 'GxVAEs consist of two joint VAEs, including MolVAE. ; GxVAEs leverages MolVAE.', 'source_index': [1, 2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'MOLVAE'}, {'weight': 7.5, 'description': 'GxVAEs are compared against DRAGONET. ; GxVAEs is compared to DRAGONET. ; GxVAEs generates molecules with higher therapeutic properties than DRAGONET. ; GxVAEs generates candidate therapeutic molecules for diseases, and DRAGONET is also used for the same purpose, implying a comparative relationship in therapeutic molecule generation for diseases.', 'source_index': [1, 2, 2, 2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'DRAGONET'}, {'weight': 7.0, 'description': "GxVAEs' performance is evaluated using metrics like Validity. ; GxVAEs has higher validity than TRIOMPHE.", 'source_index': [1, 2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'VALIDITY'}, {'weight': 7.5, 'description': "GxVAEs' Tanimoto coefficients were much higher than those of two SOTA models, and specifically for AKT1, it was 2.7 and 2.0 times higher than baselines. ; GxVAEs has higher Tanimoto coefficients than TRIOMPHE and other SOTA models. ; GxVAEs' performance is evaluated using metrics like Tanimoto Coefficients.", 'source_index': [1, 2, 2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'TANIMOTO COEFFICIENTS'}, {'weight': 8.0, 'description': 'GxVAEs is compared to TRIOMPHE as a baseline. ; GxVAEs has a validity three times higher than TRIOMPHE for generating ligand-like molecules using gene expression profiles. ; GxVAEs has a higher uniqueness than TRIOMPHE, except for PIK3CA.', 'source_index': [2, 2, 2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'TRIOMPHE'}, {'weight': 6.0, 'description': 'GxVAEs generally has higher uniqueness than TRIOMPHE.', 'source_index': [2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'UNIQUENESS'}, {'weight': 5.0, 'description': 'GxVAEs has novelty close to TRIOMPHE.', 'source_index': [2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'NOVELTY'}, {'weight': 8.0, 'description': 'GxVAEs generates therapeutic molecules for atopic dermatitis. ; GxVAEs effectively captured the structural features of drugs approved for the treatment of atopic dermatitis. ; GxVAEs generates candidate therapeutic molecules for atopic dermatitis.', 'source_index': [2, 2, 2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'ATOPIC DERMATITIS'}, {'weight': 7.666666666666667, 'description': 'GxVAEs generates therapeutic molecules for gastric cancer. ; The molecules generated by GxVAEs for treating gastric cancer showed structural features that were similar to those of known approved drugs. ; GxVAEs generates candidate therapeutic molecules for gastric cancer.', 'source_index': [2, 2, 2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': 'GASTRIC CANCER'}, {'weight': 7.666666666666667, 'description': "GxVAEs generates therapeutic molecules for Alzheimer's disease. ; The molecules generated by GxVAEs for treating Alzheimer's disease showed structural features that were similar to those of known approved drugs. ; GxVAEs generates candidate therapeutic molecules for Alzheimer's Disease.", 'source_index': [2, 2, 2], 'source': 'GXVAES', 'target': "ALZHEIMER'S DISEASE"}, {'weight': 9.4, 'description': 'ProfileVAE extracts latent features from gene expression profiles. ; ProfileVAE extracts latent features from gene expression profiles. ; ProfileVAE extracts features from gene expression profiles. ; ProfileVAE extracts features from gene expression profiles. ; ProfileVAE extracted the features of the gene expression profiles.', 'source_index': [0, 0, 1, 2, 2], 'source': 'PROFILEVAE', 'target': 'GENE EXPRESSION PROFILES'}, {'weight': 9.0, 'description': 'ProfileVAE is a variational autoencoder (VAE) within GxVAEs.', 'source_index': [0], 'source': 'PROFILEVAE', 'target': 'VARIATIONAL AUTOENCODERS (VAES)'}, {'weight': 17.0, 'description': 'ProfileVAE extracts features that serve as conditions for MolVAE. | MolVAE uses latent features extracted by ProfileVAE as conditions.', 'source_index': [0], 'source': 'PROFILEVAE', 'target': 'MOLVAE'}, {'weight': 9.0, 'description': 'MolVAE generates hit-like molecules using latent features from ProfileVAE as conditions. ; MolVAE generates hit-like molecules using features extracted from gene expression profiles as conditions. ; MolVAE, guided by features from ProfileVAE, generates hit-like molecules. ; MolVAE produces hit-like molecules using features from ProfileVAE. ; MolVAE uses features from ProfileVAE as conditions to guide the production of hit-like molecules. ; MolVAE generates Hit-like Molecules 